Description:
  Implements the final one-dimensional COMPASS deuteron A1 measurement
  through proton and neutron target components. Laboratory kinematics use
  the highest-energy prompt outgoing positive muon, excluding leptons from
  hadron decays, and require Q2 > 1 GeV2, 0.1 < y < 0.9, W > 4 GeV,
  0.004 < x < 0.7, and
  Q2 <= 100 GeV2. A Q2 > 4 GeV2 validation selection is also supplied.
  The external campaign postprocessor constructs the deuteron in an
  impulse approximation and applies 1-1.5 omegaD = 0.925 to the polarized
  numerator. D includes the muon mass and E143 R1998. The prediction
  neglects eta A2, tensor b1, binding, off-shell, and shadowing effects.
